+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+The tool registry is the validation boundary between model-produced tool input and consumer-provided executors.
+
+## Execution contract
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` validates input against the resolved tool definition's JSON Schema before invoking the
+executor. Rejected input is returned as a `ToolResponse`, with property paths and failed constraints but without
+property values, so the model can correct its call; only an unknown tool name is thrown. Extra properties are not
+removed, defaults are not applied, and accepted input reaches the executor unchanged.
+([validated by: returns actionable, value-safe rejections and passes accepted input through unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L13)).
+
+## Schema lifecycle
+
+A static tool schema is compiled when the tool is registered and reused for later executions; an invalid schema
+throws during registration with the tool name in the error.
+([validated by: compiles a static schema at registration and reuses it across executions](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L53)).
+
+A function-valued tool definition is resolved for each execution and its current schema is used for that call,
+while validators may be cached by the resolved schema object's identity.
+([validated by: validates each function-valued definition against the schema resolved for that call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L81)).
